The window bundles SolidJS (MIT), uPlot (MIT, https://github.com/leeoniya/uPlot) and the IBM Plex
fonts (SIL Open Font Licence 1.1). The desktop shell uses Tauri (MIT or Apache-2.0) and the Rust
crates listed in Cargo.lock, each under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, MPL-2.0 or Unicode
licences (checked by cargo deny, deny.toml).

The installer carries a Python runtime: CPython (PSF licence), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), SciPy
(BSD-3-Clause) and python-control (BSD-3-Clause). No GPL, LGPL or AGPL code is linked into or
bundled with Datum Sim.

The family workflow, ribbon, File page, updater and printing are taken from Datum Plan and the
Python runtime pack from Datum Plot (both MIT, same author). The engineering practices in
docs/MEMORY.md ("How we build") draw on morluto/rea (MIT); no code from it is used.

Robot descriptions (0.4.2): the engine reads URDF files with roxmltree (MIT or Apache-2.0). The
two robots that come with the app are taken, with their collision meshes, from the open
example-robot-data collection (BSD 2-Clause, LAAS-CNRS, University of Edinburgh, INRIA;
assets/robots/LICENSE-collection):
- the 6-joint industrial arm: the manufacturer's ROS description (BSD; assets/robots/arm6/SOURCE.md);
- the 7-joint arm: the manufacturer's ROS description (Apache License 2.0; assets/robots/arm7/LICENSE).
Their meshes are in ui/public/robots.

